## 1. Project Context & Business Overview
- Platform: educational **Community** for Egyptian secondary school (Thanaweya Amma). Clients: Android app (Expo), student web (Next.js), **admin web (React + Vite) — this task**. Backend: Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Storage, pg_cron). Arabic/RTL only.
- Students sign up with an Egyptian mobile number (login e-mail is derived: `01xxxxxxxxx@students.local`) with governorate, optional educational administration, **track (القسم/الشعبة)**, optional guardian phone. Each student gets a **30-day free trial** (once per phone and per Android device).
- **Access rule (single source of truth in DB: `app.student_has_access`)**: a student can see a term's content and take its exams if they are not blocked AND (their trial is running OR they hold an **active subscription for their own track + that term**). The subscription covers **the whole term — every subject (course) of the student's track in that term. There is NEVER a subscription, price or access per subject.**
- One active session per student (single device). Video links are Android-only; PDFs are **not** supported (documents are external links, e.g. Google Drive).
- Exams: central exams made of MCQ + essay questions, run in **sessions** (different audience/time per session, e.g. Giza 4 PM / Nasr City 6 PM), anonymous essay grading through Excel (the grader never sees student identity), results visible only after the **admin** approves and every session has ended.

## 2. Product Scope, Frozen Decisions, and What the Schema Does NOT Support
**Frozen decisions (from the product owner):**
- Grade level = `stages` (e.g. «الصف الثالث الثانوي»). Track/Section = `tracks` (علمي علوم / علمي رياضة / أدبي …) belonging to one stage. **There is no separate "educational stage" level above grade.**
- Hierarchy that exists: **Stage(grade) → Track(section) → Course(subject) [via `track_courses`]**, and **Term** is a global dimension (الترم الأول/الثاني). A **Lesson belongs to (Course, Term)**, a Lesson has ordered **Items** (article | link | quick_questions).
- **No Units level** (no `units` table). Lessons are a flat ordered list per (course, term). Do not build units, do not fake them with prefixes.
- **No PDF/file attachments.** Documents/videos are **links** to allowed domains (`allowed_link_domains`, kinds `video`/`document`). Only images are uploaded (bucket `content-media`).
- **Exams are linked to Course + Term** (not to a unit or lesson), run in sessions with audience filters.
- Subscription = per **track + term** (`plans`, `subscriptions`); trial = 30 days (hard-wired in DB).

**Not supported by the schema — do NOT build, document in `docs/SCHEMA_GAPS.md`:** units; PDF attachments; payment-method column (InstaPay/Vodafone Cash/bank) — only `sender_phone` + optional proof image exist; a settings table (trial length, payment instructions); cancelling a subscription (no RPC/grant; status `cancelled` exists but is unreachable); deleting/merging/changing the phone of a student; resetting a student's password (needs an Edge Function); duplicating lessons/exams atomically; server-side aggregate reports (no views/RPCs — see §13); lesson/exam reorder RPC (see §6.9 for the bulk-upsert approach).

**`is_active` caveat:** `courses.is_active` and `tracks.is_active` do **not** hide content from students (RLS looks at lesson status only). `tracks.is_active=false` only blocks choosing the track at sign-up/transfer. Label them accordingly; to hide content use lesson status `draft`/`archived`.

