## 5. Tech Stack & Engineering Rules (do not add libraries outside this list; justify any addition in `docs/DECISIONS.md` first)
React 18 + Vite + TypeScript **strict** (no `any`, no non-null `!` abuse, no `@ts-ignore`), React Router, **TanStack Query** (all server state, caching, invalidation by key factories), **TanStack Table**, **Zustand** (only for genuinely shared client state: session/roles, sidebar, wizard drafts), **React Hook Form + Zod**, **TipTap** (articles), **SheetJS (`xlsx`)**, **DOMPurify**, `@supabase/supabase-js`, `packages/design-tokens` + `packages/ui` (green g700 `#187750` for primary actions), IBM Plex Sans Arabic, Vitest + Testing Library + Playwright. **No** drag-and-drop library (reordering = move-up/move-down buttons + optional native HTML5 drag), **no** extra UI kit, **no** analytics SDK.
Architecture:
```
apps/admin/src/
  app/ (router, providers, layout)      lib/ (permissions, errors, format, xlsx, sanitize, link-domains)
  data/ client.ts (AdminApi interface + types, Zod schemas)  supabase/ (real adapter)  mock/ (adapter for tests/dev)  keys.ts (query-key factories)
  features/<module>/ (pages, components, hooks, schemas)      i18n/ar.ts
```
- **UI never calls supabase directly**; only through `AdminApi` hooks. UI = presentation; rules = DB. Zod mirrors DB constraints for early feedback only (the DB stays authoritative, its error wins).
- Pagination, sorting, search and filters are **server-side** (`range`, `order`, `ilike`, `eq`, `count: 'exact'`). Debounce search 300 ms. Never load unbounded lists.
- Uniform error pipeline: `AppError{code, message?, details?}`; Supabase/PostgREST errors normalized: DB `raise exception 'CODE…'` text → code; SQLSTATE `23503`→`FK_BLOCKED`, `23505`→`DUPLICATE`, `23514`→`CHECK_FAILED`, `42501`→`NOT_ALLOWED`, `P0001` → parse the leading CODE. One `errors.ts` Arabic map (§17). Toasts for success, inline for form errors, a blocking dialog for destructive/long operations.
- Every list/detail has **Loading (skeleton), Empty (with the next action), Error (retry)** states. Destructive/irreversible actions use a confirm dialog that states the consequence.
- Responsive 1024–1920 primary, usable at 768; accessible (keyboard, focus trap, aria-labels in Arabic, contrast). Dates in `Africa/Cairo`, Latin digits, EGP formatting «300 ج.م».
- Mock adapter must reproduce DB rules and error codes and is used for unit/e2e tests; the **Supabase adapter is the product** (see §15).

## 6. Complete Content Management Workflow (highest priority)
### 6.1 Mental model (must be visible in the UI)
`Stage (grade)` ⟶ `Track (section)` ⟶ `Course (subject)`; `Term` is chosen separately; **Lessons live under (Course, Term)**; **Items live under a Lesson**. A course may belong to several tracks (and even several stages) through `track_courses`, therefore **a lesson of that course is visible to every track that includes the course** (subject to the student's term access). The UI must always show this "audience impact".

### 6.2 Curriculum browser (`/content`)
- Left: a **tree** (collapsible): Stage → Track → Course. Each course node shows counts: lessons published/draft per term. Search box filters the tree (by stage/track/course name). Selecting a Course node opens the **course workspace** in the main pane with a **Term switcher** (tabs: الترم الأول / الترم الثاني) and the **ordered lessons list**.
- Lessons list columns: order #, title, status badge (مسودة/منشور/مؤرشف), items count (+ types icons), published_at, updated_at, actions: تعديل، معاينة، نشر/إلغاء النشر، أرشفة، تحريك لأعلى/لأسفل، حذف. Filters: status, text search (title/summary, server-side `ilike`).
- Top of workspace: breadcrumb «الصف › القسم › المادة › الترم» and the **audience banner**: «هذا المحتوى سيظهر لطلاب: [list of tracks (with stage) that include this course]». If more than one track or stage → show a warning box explaining that content is shared by all these tracks and that to separate it, a separate course must be created in Academic Structure.
- Empty states: tree empty → "ابدأ بإنشاء صف ومسار" (link; admin only); course with no lessons for the term → "أضف أول درس" (button).

### 6.3 "Add lesson" flow (dependent selects — exactly this)
Entry points: global «إضافة درس» button, and the course workspace (pre-filled). Form step 1 — **Educational context** (all required, each select depends on the previous):
1. **الصف الدراسي** (`stages`) →
2. **القسم/المسار** (`tracks` where `stage_id` = chosen; show inactive tracks greyed but selectable for content) →
3. **المادة** (`courses` joined through `track_courses` of the chosen track only) →
4. **الترم** (`terms`).
Changing an upstream select clears the downstream ones. The context persists on `lessons` only as `course_id` + `term_id` (stage/track are navigation; say so in a helper text and show the audience banner right after choosing the course).
Step 2 — **Lesson data**: `title` (2–200), `summary` (≤1000, optional), position (default = last; `sort_order` = max+1 within (course, term)), initial status = `draft`. Save → creates the lesson → redirects to the **lesson editor** where items are added. A lesson cannot be published before having items.
Errors: duplicate sort order is handled by the system (use max+1 inside a retry); `FK_BLOCKED` etc. per §17.

### 6.4 Lesson editor (`/content/lessons/:id`)
Header: context breadcrumb (read-only), title/summary inline edit, status badge, actions: معاينة (student view), نشر، إلغاء النشر، أرشفة، حذف. Body: **ordered items list** with add-item menu (3 types), move up/down, edit, delete, and per-item validation badge.
- **Item type `article`**: title (1–200) + **TipTap editor** (headings H2–H3, bold/italic, lists, links https, blockquote, images). Save **both** `body_json` (editor doc) and `body_html` (DOMPurify-sanitized HTML: allow p, h2–h4, ul, ol, li, strong, em, a[href https only], img[src only from `content-media` public URL host], br, blockquote, table family; strip everything else). Required together by the `lesson_items_shape` constraint; `url` must be null.
- **Item type `link`**: title + `url` (https). Live hint (client-side mirror of the DB check) shows the matched domain, detected kind (فيديو / مستند) and the Android-only badge for video; unmatched domain → inline error but still let the DB make the final decision. The DB sets `link_kind`/`android_only` — display them after save, never send them. Allowed domains are managed in Settings (admin). Errors: `LINK_MUST_BE_HTTPS`, `LINK_DOMAIN_NOT_ALLOWED`. Explain in the form: «الفيديوهات متاحة على تطبيق الأندرويد فقط، والمستندات (مثل Google Drive) تعمل على الجميع».
- **Item type `quick_questions`** (title only on the item; questions below): add/edit/delete/reorder questions: `prompt` (required), `explanation` (optional), options list (add/remove/reorder, text required) with a **single correct** radio (DB: partial unique index → exactly ≤1 correct; publishing requires ≥2 options and exactly 1 correct per question). Show per-question validity badges (✓ / ⚠ missing correct / ⚠ < 2 options). Student never sees the correct flag except after answering (DB/RPC concern).
- **Images**: upload (drag/paste/choose) → bucket `content-media`, path `article/<new-uuid>/<file>`; client-side checks: jpeg/png/webp, ≤ 5 MB (`FILE_TYPE_NOT_ALLOWED`/`FILE_TOO_LARGE`), progress bar, insert public URL into editor; delete from storage when removed (best effort).
- Autosave is **not** used; explicit «حفظ» with dirty-state indicator and unsaved-changes guard on navigation.

### 6.5 Publishing rules (enforced by DB trigger; UI pre-validates and shows the checklist)
Publish checklist (computed in UI, DB decides): (a) lesson has ≥ 1 item; (b) every quick-question has ≥ 2 options and exactly 1 correct; (c) every `quick_questions` item has ≥ 1 question. Failure codes: `LESSON_HAS_NO_ITEMS`, `QUICK_QUESTION_INVALID`, `QUICK_QUESTIONS_ITEM_EMPTY` → show the checklist with the failing row highlighted. Publish sets `status='published'` and `published_at`. **Unpublish** → back to `draft`; **Archive** → `archived` (hidden from students, kept for history). A published lesson stays editable, but warn: «التعديل يظهر للطلاب فورًا».

### 6.6 Preview before publishing
«معاينة» opens a read-only **student-style rendering** of the lesson built from the admin's own data (same sanitizer): article HTML, document links (new tab), video links shown as «متاح على تطبيق الأندرويد» card, quick questions interactive in-memory (shows correct answer + explanation after choosing; **no DB writes, no progress**). A banner «وضع المعاينة» is always visible.

### 6.7 Deletion & integrity rules (pre-check in UI, DB is final)
- Delete **item**: confirm; cascades its quick questions/options and students' progress/answers for it → say so in the dialog (show counts from `item_progress`/`quick_answers` if readable by role).
- Delete **lesson**: allowed (cascades items/progress). If the lesson is published and has student progress → strong warning + suggest **Archive** instead.
- Delete **course/track/stage/term/plan/governorate/administration**: the DB uses `ON DELETE RESTRICT` where data depends on it. Before deleting, run dependency count queries and show «لا يمكن الحذف لأنه مرتبط بـ: 12 درس، 3 امتحانات…» with the buttons disabled; if a race makes the DB reject, map `FK_BLOCKED` to the same style message. Deleting a `track_courses` link is allowed but warn that students of that track immediately lose that subject's lessons/exams.
- Never offer delete for: students, attempts, results, subscriptions, payments, audit log.

### 6.8 Search & filter inside content
Global content search box (title/summary of lessons, scoped to the selected course/term or across all with filters stage/track/course/term/status), server-side, paginated, results show the full breadcrumb and open the editor.

### 6.9 Ordering
`sort_order` uniqueness (lessons per (course,term); items per lesson; quick questions per item; options per question; exam questions per exam) is **DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED**. Reordering = ONE request that updates the whole affected list: PostgREST bulk `upsert` with `onConflict: 'id'` sending **all NOT NULL columns of each row** (e.g. for lessons: `id, course_id, term_id, title, sort_order`) so the constraint is checked at statement end. On failure, refetch and show `REORDER_FAILED`. Record in `SCHEMA_GAPS.md` that a dedicated reorder RPC would be safer.

