- **Tracks (الأقسام/المسارات)** — `stage_id`, `name_ar` (unique per stage), `is_active`, `sort_order`; filter by stage; shows #students, #courses; deactivate = cannot be chosen at sign-up/transfer (explain). Delete blocked by students/plans/subscriptions/payments.
- **Courses (المواد)** — `name_ar` (**globally unique**), `icon_key` (choose from a fixed icon set defined in design-tokens; free text not allowed), `sort_order`, `is_active` (display flag, caveat §2). Detail tab **"المسارات"**: manage `track_courses` (add/remove track with per-track `sort_order`), grouped by stage. Show which tracks use it and the audience-impact warning when linking a course already used elsewhere.
- **Terms (الترمات)** — fixed global entries with `name_ar` (unique), `sort_order`, **`access_ends_at`** (when purchased access for that term stops; **must be set each year before approving payments**, else `TERM_ACCESS_END_NOT_SET`). Show a red banner on Dashboard/Payments when a term has no future `access_ends_at`.
- **Governorates / Administrations** (Settings): governorates (27 seeded) editable; administrations per governorate (`name_ar` unique per governorate, `is_active`). Bulk import of administrations from Excel (columns: `governorate`, `administration`) — validate in browser, insert in one request, report duplicates.
- Relationship view: a read-only **matrix** page "تغطية المنهج": rows = tracks (grouped by stage), columns = courses, cell = ✓ (linked) with lesson counts per term (published/draft). Used for QA of content coverage.

## 8. Subscription & Pricing Business Logic
**Core rule (put it in the UI copy and in code comments):** subscription = **track × term**, covers **all courses** of that track in that term. No per-course price or subscription anywhere.
- **Plans** (`plans`): one price per (track, term): `track_id`, `term_id`, `price_egp > 0`, `is_active`; **exactly one active plan per (track, term)** (partial unique index). Screen "الأسعار": a **pricing matrix** — rows = tracks grouped by stage (grade), columns = terms; each cell = active price or «غير مسعّر» with «إضافة سعر». Actions: add (creates active plan), edit price (confirm: «لن يؤثر على الاشتراكات السابقة»; history is preserved because requests/subscriptions store a price snapshot), deactivate (then the track-term can't be purchased: students see `NO_PLAN_FOR_TRACK_TERM`), delete only if never used (`FK_BLOCKED` otherwise). Price must be > 0.
- **Trial**: 30 days from sign-up, once per phone and per device (DB trigger). Read-only explanation in Settings; **not configurable**. Admin tools: `extend_trial(student, days 1..365)`.
- **Subscription lifecycle** (`subscriptions`): created by **approve_payment** (price snapshot, `ends_at` = `p_ends_at` or `terms.access_ends_at`) or by **grant_subscription** (manual, price 0, note). No overlapping `active` subscription for the same student+term (`ALREADY_SUBSCRIBED`). Expiry: pg_cron flips `active → expired` hourly after `ends_at`. Renewal = the student pays again for the next term (or, if expired, same term with a new `access_ends_at`); there is no cancel (gap).
- **Subscriptions list** (read; students_manager/payments_reviewer/support): filters status, term, track, stage, date ranges (starts/ends), search by student name/phone (via joined profile), amount; columns: student, track, term, price paid, starts, ends, status, source (payment request / manual grant + note). Row action: open student; **«منح اشتراك»** (students_manager) from student page: term select (only terms with plans or any term? → any term), `ends_at` defaulting to the term's `access_ends_at` (required, must be in the future), note.
- Students with expired/active status: surfaced in Students list filters («اشتراك ساري»، «منتهي»، «في التجربة»، «تجربة منتهية بلا اشتراك»).

## 9. Payments Management
- Student submits `payment_requests` (term, sender phone, optional proof). **Amount is copied from the active plan of the student's track+term by the DB, never from the client.** Statuses: `pending → approved | rejected` (final).
- **Queue** (`v_payment_queue`, payments_reviewer): tabs معلّق (default, oldest first) / مقبول / مرفوض; filters: term, track, date range, search (student name/phone, sender phone); columns: created, student, phone, track, term, amount, sender phone, proof (thumb), status, reviewer/date, reject reason. Server-side pagination.
- **Review drawer**: student info (name, phone, governorate, track, trial/subscriptions summary, previous requests count), expected amount, sender phone (copy button), proof image via **signed URL** from private bucket `payment-proofs` (zoom/rotate; «لا يوجد إيصال» when absent), **Approve** (optional `p_ends_at` override, defaults to term access end; if the term has none → blocker message telling an admin to set it) and **Reject** (reason required, ≥1 char, shown to the student). Both confirm dialogs. After success: row moves tabs, subscription link shown, student is notified by the DB.
- Errors: `REQUEST_ALREADY_REVIEWED` (refresh row, explain who reviewed), `TERM_ACCESS_END_NOT_SET`, `ALREADY_SUBSCRIBED`, `REJECT_REASON_REQUIRED`, `REQUEST_NOT_FOUND`.
- Payment methods: the schema has no method column. Show only what exists; document the gap.
- Payment history per student (in student page) and CSV/XLSX export of the filtered queue.

## 10. Students Management
- **List** (`v_students_overview`, security_invoker): columns name, phone, guardian phone, governorate, administration, track, trial state (باقٍ N يوم / منتهية), active subscriptions count, blocked badge, created. Server-side search (name/phone), filters: governorate, administration (depends on governorate), stage, track, status (trial/subscribed/expired/blocked), created range; sort; page size 25/50/100; export (current filter).
- **Student page tabs:** (1) البيانات — profile fields (read-only phone), actions below; (2) الاشتراكات والمدفوعات; (3) النشاط — `item_progress` summary and `quick_answers` (students_manager); (4) الامتحانات — attempts (status, started/submitted) and results (exams/students_manager); (5) الأجهزة والجلسات — `device_sessions` (support/students_manager).
- **Actions:** extend trial (1–365 days) · block/unblock (reason optional; blocking ends sessions immediately) · change track (target must be an **active** track; warn that content/exam access switches immediately and old-track subscriptions don't cover the new track) · change governorate/administration (`update_student_location`; administrations list depends on governorate) · reset device session (support) · grant manual subscription (students_manager). Each needs a confirm dialog and writes the audit log (DB does it). Roles gate each action.
- Not available (gaps): delete student, edit phone, reset password.
- **Announcements link:** from a filtered list → «أرسل إعلانًا لهذه المجموعة» is **not** supported (announcement filters are only track/governorate); only offer sending by track/governorate in the Announcements module.

## 11. Exams & Question Management (`exams` role)
**Model:** `exams` (course, term, title, description, `duration_minutes` 5–300, `late_entry_minutes` 0–60 default 30, `disconnect_grace_seconds` 30–1800 default 300, `status` draft/published/archived) → `exam_questions` (position, type mcq|essay, `prompt_html`, `points` > 0) → `question_options` (MCQ only, exactly one correct) ; `exam_sessions` (name, `starts_at`, `ends_at` auto = start + duration) → `session_audience` rows (governorate / administration / track; null = any; **most specific match wins**).
### 11.1 Exam builder (wizard with save-as-you-go drafts)
1. **Basics** — dependent selects Stage → Track → Course (from `track_courses`) → Term (exam stores `course_id` + `term_id`), title, description, duration, late-entry window, disconnect grace. Audience banner: tracks that include the course (the DB requires the course to belong to ≥ 1 track at publish: `COURSE_NOT_IN_ANY_TRACK`).
2. **Questions** — list with reorder; add MCQ (prompt via TipTap-lite: bold/italic/lists/images, points, 2–6 options, exactly one correct) or essay (prompt, points; **no options**: `ESSAY_CANNOT_HAVE_OPTIONS`); duplicate-question helper is client-side only (creates a new row); total points shown. Excel bulk import (§11.3).
3. **Sessions & audience** — add sessions (name, start datetime, end shown read-only = start + duration; **must start in the future**: `SESSION_MUST_START_IN_FUTURE`) and audience rows per session (governorate, optional administration, optional track). Warn on ambiguity (two sessions equally specific for the same students → `AMBIGUOUS_AUDIENCE`) and show a **coverage preview**: for each governorate × track the matched session (computed with the same specificity rule) and counts of students per session from `profiles` counts, plus a list of eligible students matched to **no** session.
4. **Review & Publish** — checklist: ≥1 question, MCQ validity, ≥1 session, every session has audience, no ambiguity, course in a track. Publish → `status='published'` (DB trigger decides; show returned code).
- **Lock**: once any session has started the exam content is frozen (`EXAM_LOCKED`): UI switches to read-only with a «مقفول» badge; only archive and viewing remain. Never offer editing/deleting questions/sessions after lock (and don't hide the DB error if reached).
### 11.2 Monitoring (`v_exam_session_stats`, exams)
Per session: total attempts, in-progress, submitted, auto-submitted; auto-refresh every 15 s while a session is live; eligible-student count vs attempts (participation %). No student identities on this screen for the `exams` role (profiles are not readable by that role).
### 11.3 Excel import of questions
Template download with columns `type (mcq|essay), prompt, points, option_1..option_6, correct_option (1–6)`. Validate fully in browser (type, points > 0, MCQ 2–6 options, exactly one correct, essay without options, max 500 rows); show an errors table with row numbers; nothing is saved if any row fails. Save = insert questions (one request) then options (one request); if the second fails, delete the just-inserted questions (compensating rollback) and report. Rejected after lock.
### 11.4 Statistics
`question_stats(exam)`: attempts, answered, correct, % correct (MCQ), average essay score; flag questions < 20 % or > 95 % correct; score distribution from `exam_results` (after approval).

## 12. Grading & Results Management
**Flow (grader exports → grades offline/AI in Excel → grader imports → admin approves):**
1. **Preconditions:** every session of the exam has ended (`SESSIONS_NOT_ENDED` otherwise); results not yet approved (`ALREADY_APPROVED`).
2. **Export** (`export_grading`, grader): creates a batch, auto-submits leftovers, returns rows **with only** `answer_code` (anonymous), question position/text, answer text, max points, current score. Build XLSX columns **in this exact order**: `answer_code, question_position, question_text, answer_text, max_points, score` (score prefilled with current score). **No identity data anywhere.** Show batch id/time in history (`grading_batches`).
3. **Import** (`import_grades(batch, rows, ai_flag)`): parse XLSX/CSV in browser; accept comma or dot decimals and Arabic-Indic digits (normalize); show a preview table with row-level validation before sending; checkbox «تم التصحيح بالذكاء الاصطناعي» (stored as `ai_graded`). All-or-nothing: on `IMPORT_REJECTED` render the DB's row/error list (`UNKNOWN_ANSWER_CODE, UNKNOWN_ESSAY_QUESTION, NO_ANSWER_FOR_THIS_QUESTION, INVALID_SCORE, SCORE_ABOVE_MAX, DUPLICATE_ROW, EMPTY_OR_INVALID_FILE`) and save nothing. Re-import overwrites per answer.
4. **Approval** (`approve_grading`, **admin only**): shows pre-flight summary (attempts, essay answers graded/ungraded, AI-graded flag, sessions ended) → confirm → creates `exam_results` for every finished attempt (including auto-submitted) → locks the exam's grading (`ALREADY_APPROVED`), notifies students. Blocked with `UNGRADED_ANSWERS: N` (show N and how to fix).
5. **After approval** (admin): «مراجعة المقالي» — `list_essay_answers` (shows student name; admin only) + `adjust_essay_grade(answer, score, reason)` (reason ≥ 3 chars, score ≤ max) recomputing the result; audited.
6. Graders (role `grader`) only see Export/Import and batch history; `exams` role sees batches + results read-only.
**Results screen** (`exam_results`, exams/students_manager): per exam table (student, MCQ, essay, total, max, %, AI flag), search/sort/filter, XLSX export, distribution chart (plain SVG), and student-level link. Results are visible to students only after approval **and** all sessions ended (informational).

## 13. Dashboard & Reporting
**No server aggregation exists** (no views/RPCs for sums). Use: (a) `count: 'exact', head: true` queries for counts; (b) for money and trends, fetch filtered rows page by page (cap 20,000 rows; if exceeded show «النتائج مقتطعة — ضيّق الفترة») and aggregate in the browser; document in `SCHEMA_GAPS.md`.
- **Dashboard cards (role-aware):** pending payments (+oldest age) · students in trial / trial ending in 7 days · active subscriptions by term · students blocked · live/upcoming exam sessions (next 24 h) · attempts in progress · exams awaiting grading/approval · lessons draft vs published · terms with missing `access_ends_at` (alert) · last 10 audit events (admin).
- **Reports (`/reports`)**, all with date range, term/track/stage filters, table + XLSX export: 1) **Revenue** — approved payments & subscriptions: total EGP, by term, by track/stage, by month, manual grants count (price 0) shown separately; 2) **Subscriptions** — active/expired/ending soon, renewal funnel (trial → paid) per term; 3) **Payments** — approval/rejection rate, avg review time, top reject reasons; 4) **Students** — sign-ups per day, by governorate/administration/track, trial conversion; 5) **Content coverage** — lessons per course/term/status, courses without published lessons; 6) **Exam participation & results** — attempts vs eligible, average score per exam/session, question difficulty; 7) **Engagement** — item completion rates per lesson (`item_progress`), quick-question accuracy (`quick_answers`).
Charts: simple SVG components (bar/line) built in `packages/ui`; every chart has a data table fallback.

