## 15. API & Supabase Integration Requirements
- Implement `data/client.ts` (`AdminApi`) with one method per row of §14; implement `data/supabase/*` for real (`supabase.from(...)`, `supabase.rpc(...)`, storage); keep `data/mock/*` for tests with identical behavior/error codes. Env: `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `VITE_DATA_MODE=mock|supabase`. **Never** use the service-role key in the browser.
- Auth: e-mail + password via Supabase Auth; **TOTP MFA** (Supabase MFA) mandatory for `admin` and `payments_reviewer`; idle timeout 30 min (warn at 28); sign-out clears all query caches and Zustand stores.
- Query keys by factory (`keys.students.list(filters)`); every mutation invalidates the exact affected keys (e.g., approving a payment invalidates payment queue, subscriptions, dashboard counts, student detail).
- Edge Function `create-staff` is specified only; UI calls it via `supabase.functions.invoke`; handle `NOT_FOUND`/non-deployed gracefully.
- Date/time: always send ISO with offset; show in Africa/Cairo.
- Contract tests (`tests/contract/*`): run the Supabase adapter against a local Supabase (`supabase start`, apply `supabase/migrations/*`, `seed.sql`) with test users per role; assert each §14 row (success + one denial + one constraint error). If Docker is unavailable, mark them skipped and say so in the report.

## 16. UI/UX Requirements
Design tokens only; RTL-correct icons/chevrons; dense but readable tables (TanStack Table, sticky header, column visibility, server pagination); consistent page frame (title, breadcrumbs, primary action at the left in RTL); forms with inline errors (Zod + server codes), disabled-submit while pending, unsaved-changes guard; confirm dialogs name the object and the consequence; toasts auto-dismiss, errors persistent until closed; keyboard shortcuts limited to Esc/Enter in dialogs; copy buttons for phones/ids; skeletons not spinners; empty states always suggest the next action; print-friendly CSS not required. Arabic copy is concise, professional, gender-neutral.

