## 18. Security & RLS Requirements
- Trust the DB; **never** implement authorization only in React. Each mutation goes through the table/RPC that enforces the role; the UI additionally hides/guards by the §3 matrix.
- Anonymity: the `grader` and `exams` roles must never receive student identity in grading screens; only `admin` sees names in essay review. Do not join profiles on those screens.
- No secrets in the bundle/repo; no PII in URLs, logs, `localStorage` (only UI prefs); proof images only via short-lived signed URLs; HTML always sanitized before `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`; CSP-friendly (no inline scripts); idle timeout + MFA as above; sign-out invalidates caches.
- Audit: the DB writes `audit_log` inside RPCs; the UI exposes it read-only (admin) with filters action/entity/actor/date and XLSX export.
- Staff management: assign multiple roles; the last admin cannot be removed (`LAST_ADMIN`); an admin cannot remove their own admin role if they are the last.

